Tried 2026-11-27 (twins-on-several-targets round), dropped.

What: targets.ts subSkillEvent and its use in castassembly.ts assembleCasts (and loggedCastFates' `sub-skill` fate,
the EVENT line's words): in a fight read per target, a logged cast event at the ms of a hit of its operator whose key
is the skill's id with a suffix no kit hit lists is a sub-skill's cast, no press, left out of every pass. The case:
Camille's Vesperwings moving to the next slug when its own dies (abilityrange_first's listen_target_dead →
reset_target → projhit_sub → normal_skill_abilityrange, the battle skill's damage, Heat infliction and
Susceptibility on the next target); ZMDLogs logs a normal_skill event at four of its six such hits (6339 19.68,
24.55, 29.67 s; 7b54 16.59 s), the fire Susceptibility listed since each hit's ms. Over every development log the only
other such events are Purrchena's (04d4, 99fb), presses of keys her kit lacks.

Measured (npm run measure -- --base HEAD --logs 6339,7b54,9c6e, on top of the round's twins):
  6339 plain 115 → 103, −10.3 → −15.2% (the twins alone: 115, −10.3%); 7b54, 9c6e as with the twins alone.

Why dropped: the press the replay made at each event stood in for the move: its landing 0.4 s later has the same
damage (9287 against the logged 9287) and gives the next slug the Susceptibility and the Heat infliction Laevatain
absorbs (her Melting Flame at 32.24 s is a stack short already: the 35.70 s empowered hit is log-only). Without the
move's own landing, leaving the events out loses that state. What it needs: a kit hit for the move (key
normal_skill_abilityrange, the battle skill's scale, Heat infliction, the Vesperwings buff) landed by the replay at
each logged move (or at a logged kill of the target carrying her Vesperwings, targets.ts knows which), with no press:
packages/data's Camille kit and a replay-side "entity landing" cast, neither in this round's files. Then this diff
applies on top.

